    "done_when": "A dispatch that names no lane must reach the picker even when the local lane is congested. Local-lane load is something Jev weighs, not a refusal that pre-empts it. A named --local keeps the refusal.\n\nMeasured 2026-10-07 at 05:26Z: reckon crew dispatch with no lane named (route picker) returned error \"lane-paused\": \"the lane's router grants 0 extra workers to session s25-picker (the session's own worker slots); the router's own verdict is congested — admission headroom is -1\". It came back with no picker_selection, so Jev never ran. Codex had just reset to full and was available. The lead's routing rule (dotfiles 063d530) makes no-lane dispatch the default, so this refusal turns every no-lane dispatch into a failure whenever the local lane is busy, and sessions will drift back to naming lanes.\n\n1. Find where the local-lane admission gate (_dispatch_lane_gate and the lane-paused refusal in reckon/crew/dispatch.py) runs relative to the picker for a picker-routed dispatch, and say so in the manifest.\n2. For a picker-routed dispatch, run the pick first, with local_lane admission, headroom, worker slots and expected wait in its inputs, as the picker already receives them:\n   - if Jev routes to the local lane, apply the local admission gate to that choice. A congested lane then refuses with the same remedy text, or holds if that is how the picker records it;\n   - if Jev routes to a metered lane, the local gate does not apply;\n   - if Jev holds, record the hold as today.\n   A named --local or --backend keeps today's order and refusal exactly.\n3. Tests in tests/test_congested_local_lane_still_reaches_the_picker.py, using a fixture lane document that reports congestion (admission headroom -1, session slots 0):\n   - a no-lane dispatch with a stub picker that routes to a metered backend launches on it;\n   - a stub that routes to the local lane gets the lane-paused refusal;\n   - a stub that holds records a hold;\n   - a --local dispatch is refused before any pick, as today.\n\nGate: tests/test_picker*.py, tests/test_dispatch_lane*.py, tests/test_lane*.py, tests/test_routing*.py and the new test file. Run them with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log for base and one for head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
